cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying Experiment II dataset, please
  cite this archived release.
type: software
title: >-
  Multi-Robot Coordination for Emergency Evacuation via Adversarial
  Reinforcement Learning with Complex Crowd Behavior and Dynamic Hazard Modeling
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-11
repository-code: https://github.com/HaitianMu/MultiRobot_ARL_2025
url: https://github.com/HaitianMu/MultiRobot_ARL_2025/releases/tag/v1.0.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Unity and ML-Agents implementation of an adversarial reinforcement learning
  framework for multi-robot emergency evacuation, including the curated final
  V11 Experiment II evaluation dataset, frozen policies, training configuration,
  seed-level statistics, and a qualitative scene-level trajectory example.
keywords:
  - adversarial reinforcement learning
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - multi-robot coordination
  - emergency evacuation
  - crowd behavior
  - zero-shot transfer
  - Unity ML-Agents
